{
 "schema": 1,
 "_comment": [
  "Port-sync gate rows for tools/extract_baseline.py. These live here, not in",
  "the tool, so the rows are data rather than code. This file is shipped BOTH in the checkout's tools/ and beside the script in the windows-shell-dev skill; the skill copy is the one that survives a sandbox reset, so keep the two in sync. Rows are maintained by whoever adds the feature.",
  "needs re-shipping when DCX.bat grows a feature. Add a row per feature that",
  "must survive into the Python port.",
  "required_streams: [label, [form, ...args]] - args match as a subsequence of",
  "the extracted Cmd, so redirects/placeholders do not have to be spelled out.",
  "Labels are mechanical: a stream ends at the NEXT label, internal jump targets included. So a command written after an internal ':_' label is owned by that label (e.g. _tw_ib_addput, _tw_pa_ns_ok), not by the screen above it. Same distinction sincript's Get-RoutineBody needed.",
  "Rows follow the code, not the other way round. Two examples worth keeping in mind: _tw_pa_ns_ok and _tw_qs_put now write through a single-quoted device payload ('!_sv!') because bare values were being quote-stripped by adb, and the quick-settings put moved out of _tw_qs_addput into :_tw_qs_put when that path was refactored. A row that names a label the code no longer uses fails loudly, which is the point - but it must then be updated here in the same pass, or the gate stays red and stops meaning anything."
 ],
